<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ terms of trade fell 0.7 pct in June qtr.</title>
<headline>NZ terms of trade fell 0.7 pct in June qtr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand (SNZ) on Wednesday released the following provisional overseas trade, price, volume and terms of trade indices for the June 1996 qtr.</p>
<p>			     (percentage)</p>
<p>			 June 1996   March 1995  June 1995</p>
<p>Terms of Trade	-0.7	   -1.4	   -2.2</p>
<p>Export Price Index  -2.1	   -1.2	   -3.9</p>
<p>Import price Index  -1.4	   +0.2	   -1.8</p>
<p>Import price changes (percentage) from previous qtr</p>
<p>				    June quarter  March quarter</p>
<p>    Food and beverages	   +4.0	     -2.0</p>
<p>    Petroleum and products     -9.2	    +16.4</p>
<p>    Non-fuel crude materials   -0.7	     +0.9</p>
<p>    Pastics, plastic articles  -1.0	     -8.0</p>
<p>    Textile yarn, fabric	 -4.3	     -6.6</p>
<p>    Iron and steel		 -2.7	     -2.5</p>
<p>    Non-electrical machinery   -1.6		0.0</p>
<p>    Electrical machinery	 +0.7	     +1.8</p>
<p>    Transport equipment	  -2.7	     +1.5</p>
<p>		Main export price changes  (percentage)</p>
<p>				    June quarter  March quarter</p>
<p>    Dairy products		 -8.6	     +0.7</p>
<p>    Meat, wool, byproducts     -1.4	     -0.6</p>
<p>    Fish, fish preparations    +1.3	     +2.2</p>
<p>    Food and beverages	   -1.4	     -0.2</p>
<p>    Forestry products	    -8.5	     -5.7</p>
<p>    Non-fuel crude materials   -5.4	     -2.7</p>
<p>    Aluminium			-1.6	     -7.4</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
